 budget last autumn  where i said yes have we had to make  some difficult decisions we have i  believe those are the right decisions  there are responsible divisions  decisions for the country's economic  security going forward  but those are done now and my priority  is to reduce people's taxes we started  at the budget and you talked about those  on the lowest incomes earlier the first  tax cut we put in place was on people on  universal credit they face quite a high  tax rate when they're going back into  work we cut that significantly it's a  two billion pound tax cut for millions  of people it will mean a single mother  for example working full-time on the  national living wage will be 1200 pounds  better off so that was the first tax cut  and my priority over time is to keep  cutting people's taxes get that bar down  um and and and that's where we're gonna  head um just finally will boris johnson  lead the conservatives into the next  election yes thank you
 

